    "marketSession": "CLOSED",
    "summary": "Supplemental close review: Indian equities rebounded on 13 October and IT led, but the move followed improved sentiment after the Finance Minister said she would hear market participants on LTCG/STT; no formal tax proposal was announced. HCLTech’s Q2 FY27 INR revenue rose 11.5% year on year, while constant-currency growth was 2.6%; FY27 constant-currency revenue guidance is 2.5–4.0%. That is constructive, but not a reason to chase a one-day rally. September CPI was provisionally 5.54% and food inflation 7.74%, both higher than August. Plan: add HCLTech and large IT to the research watchlist, and check current valuations before any purchase. A broad index fund can be considered for staged deployment after checking costs and tracking; no trade was executed and the ₹10,000 tranche remains available.",
